-- title:
--   Transversality of consecutive components at each edge point
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a Deligne–Rapoport model package $\mathfrak{X}$ for $p$, a discrete valuation ring $O$ which is a domain whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$ (hypothesis $h\varpi$), an algebraically closed field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$. Assume $H$, the bundle [`V3Asm.SiteHyps`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L267) of site hypotheses (finiteness of the node set, existence of oriented crossing charts, the étale-neighbourhood data, injectivity of $n \mapsto x_n$ and closedness of each $\{x_n\}$, and the model hypotheses on $O$), and assume $h\xi$: each of the points $\xi_j$ lies in the open set $X_0$ of the chart input [`V3Asm.C`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L280), that is, in the complement of the union of the marked points $x_n$. Write $Y$ for the scheme glued from this data, $\mathrm{width}$ for the thickness function of the chart input, $\mathrm{comp}$ for the resulting family of ideal sheaf data on $Y$ indexed by the component set $\mathtt{X0MqComponents}\,\mathrm{width}$, and $\mathrm{edgePt}$ for the associated edge points. The assertion is: for every node $n$ and every $d \in \mathrm{Fin}(\mathrm{width}\,n)$ there are an affine open $U \subseteq Y$ containing $x := \mathrm{edgePt}(n,d)$ such that the image, under the germ map $\Gamma(Y,U) \to \mathcal{O}_{Y,x}$, of the ideal $\mathrm{comp}(\mathrm{chainPos}(n,d))(U) + \mathrm{comp}(\mathrm{chainPos}(n,d+1))(U)$ is the whole maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{Y,x}$. Here $\mathrm{chainPos}(n,d)$ is $\mathrm{Sum.inl}\,0$ for $d = 0$, the exceptional index $\mathrm{Sum.inr}(n,d-1)$ for $0 < d < \mathrm{width}\,n$, and $\mathrm{Sum.inl}\,1$ otherwise, so the two ideals are those of the two consecutive members of the chain at $n$ meeting at that edge point.
--
--   This records the transversality of the special fibre of the resolved model at the double points of its chain of components: at each edge point the local equations of the two components through it generate the maximal ideal of the local ring, so the point is an ordinary double point. It is one of the conditions verified in the construction of the resolved Deligne–Rapoport model package, and is used by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts).
